    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored by **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.72) and **James Wood** (69.20), both of whom benefit significantly from facing Merrill Kelly\u2019s inflated 5.31 xERA. **Tyler Soderstrom** stands out as the day's high-water mark; his positioning in the #2 spot, paired with a favorable platoon advantage, creates an ideal high-leverage environment for counting stats. **James Wood** is similarly positioned for a massive ceiling, as he combines top-tier xwOBA with a +14% park factor boost at the top of the order. While **Austin Riley** (64.88) provides a strong, high-floor presence at UTIL, he carries the only significant weather risk of the day\u2014a 35% chance of rain that could shorten his night against Michael King.\n\nWe continue to prioritize elite speed profiles despite the volatility, which keeps **Corbin Carroll** (58.95) in the mix even on a day where the matchup against Gage Jump presents a platoon penalty. His base projection remains high enough to justify the start, though he sits significantly lower than **Vinnie Pasquantino** (67.63), whose +14% platoon edge against an average starter makes him one of the safest bets on the board. The most difficult bench decision involved **Josh Naylor** (59.33); he was the first man out, narrowly edged by the higher upside of our starting infielders. While **Josh Naylor** had a solid profile, his poor BvP history against Brady Singer and a slight park factor drag pushed the optimizer to favor the offensive environment surrounding **Max Muncy** (63.29) and **Jose Caballero** (60.94).\n\nManagers should keep a close eye on the final lineup cards. With **Dalton Rushing**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Max Muncy**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **James Wood**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **Austin Riley** all carrying \"Lineup Pending\" designations, our aggregate score is sensitive to potential late-afternoon adjustments. **Brice Turang** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** remain our confirmed anchors. While we remain thin on the bench\u2014excluding **Zach McKinstry**, **Travis Bazzana**, and **Cole Young**\u2014we are positioned to capitalize on favorable xERA matchups across the board, provided the weather in the **Austin Riley** game remains manageable.",
